    "evidence": "Apply the 10% deployment threshold: the 2026-10-19 full supply feed assigns Berachain 66.5305% and Ethereum 33.3848%; all other chains are individually sub-threshold. Verified Ethereum 0x09d4214c03d01f49544c0448dbe3a27f768f2b34 is immutable Stablecoin (AccessControl, ERC20Burnable), with MINTER-only issuance and allowance-gated burnFrom, no blacklist, freeze, seizure, transfer pause, forced holder burn or proxy upgrade. At Ethereum block 26224766 (2026-10-19T06:15:23Z), EIP1967 implementation/admin slots are zero. Verified direct Berachain RusdOft at the same address is vanilla OFT/ERC20: its owner changes bridge routing, not local-holder transfers or balances; it has no token-upgrade path. Tempo 0x20c0000000000000000000007f7ba549dd0251b9 does retain a direct mutable TIP20 policy/pause/blocked-burn surface: at block 44841241 (2026-10-19T06:15:29Z), paused=false, transferPolicyId=1, and DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE is held by Reservoir EOA 0xb7570e32ded63b25163369d5eb4d8e89e70e5602. Its totalSupply is only 10 raw at 6 decimals. The complete circulating feed gives its share as 4.4123353881e-09% and independent native supply reads confirm it is far below 10%, so those peripheral controls do not set the verdict. Other examined EVM OFTs have ordinary ERC20 transfers, and the examined Solana mint has no freeze authority; no material direct holder control is established. rUSD has no declared parent. Its issuer reserve API fetched 2026-10-19 reports totalAssets USD 111301098.149388476156764562, exactly the sum of all 16 disclosed rows. Keeping every row in that denominator, named USDC, USDT, USD1 and AUSD cash/lending/vault claims alone contribute 93.39916506% issuer-freezable exposure. GHO, Agua and the newly observed USDG vault are conservatively excluded from the numerator; no assumption about their controls is needed. Thus reserves strictly exceed 50% and the materiality-scoped verdict is Upstream, not Yes. The API provides no independent composition timestamp.",
    "reviewer": "FreezeWatch full-dataset review 2026-10-19",
    "reviewedAt": "2026-10-19"
